---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import data from '../../data/funding.json';

// Where the funding list comes from, in one place. The main page used to
// carry this as a row of chips ("weekly trawl", "prior-sightings ledger")
// that named the parts without saying what any of them was. This page says
// what each one is, and links the data behind it.
const unverified = data.watchlist.filter((w) => (w.url_verified || '').toUpperCase() !== 'Y').length;
const categories = [...new Set(data.watchlist.map((w) => w.category).filter(Boolean))].length;
---

<Layout title="Funding sources | Zhiqian Chen">
  <main class="container">
    <Nav current="funding" />

    <article class="doc">
      <p class="back"><a href="/funding"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left" aria-hidden="true"></i> Computing Funding</a></p>
      <h1>Sources and data</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The list is rebuilt twice a week, on Monday and Friday. A research agent sweeps the sources below,
        opens every call at its own page to read the deadline, the amount and who may apply, and writes a brief.
        A scheduled job then turns the brief into this site, keeping only what is true for anyone and dropping
        anything personal. Latest sweep: <b>{data.date}</b>.
      </p>

      <h2>What is swept</h2>
      <ol class="layers">
        <li>
          <h3>Every new federal and New York State listing</h3>
          <p>
            All opportunities posted in the past seven days on
            <a href="https://simpler.grants.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">simpler.grants.gov</a>, from every agency,
            plus forecasts created in that window, each one opened and kept if universities may apply. The same
            for New York State on <a href="https://grantsmanagement.ny.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NYS Grants Management</a>
            and Empire State Development's requests for proposals. This is the safety net: it catches calls from
            agencies nobody thought to check.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>A fixed checklist of agency funding pages</h3>
          <p>
            Over a hundred programme pages read on every sweep and reported either way, new call or nothing new:
            NSF across its directorates, NIH institutes and notices, DOE, DARPA, ONR, AFOSR, AFRL, ARO, NIST,
            NASA, NOAA, DHS, IES, NEH, IMLS, ARPA-H and ARPA-E among them, and in New York, NYSERDA, Empire State
            Development and Empire AI.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>The funder watchlist</h3>
          <p>
            {data.counts.watchlist} funders in {categories} categories, checked on every sweep whether or not they
            have announced anything: foundations, companies' academic programmes and the smaller niche funders a
            search would miss. Built by hand, partly from the funding acknowledgements on computing faculty pages
            reached through <a href="https://csrankings.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CSRankings</a>.
            {unverified > 0 && <> {unverified} of its links are not yet confirmed.</>}
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Announcements of new money</h3>
          <p>
            New philanthropies and new corporate research programmes in AI, AI-safety funder bulletins, and the
            Computing Community Consortium blog. These land in the early signals until a real call appears.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>How a call is read</h2>
      <p>
        Deadlines and amounts come from the call's own page, never from memory or a summary. Award sizes use the
        ceiling and floor on the grants.gov listing, or the budget in the NSF solicitation. A call counts as new only
        if it is not already in the registry below, so a programme seen in March is not announced again in October.
      </p>

      <h2>The data</h2>
      <ul class="files">
        <li>
          <a class="file" href="/funding/data.json">data.json</a>
          <span>Everything on the funding page as one file: the {data.counts.opportunities} calls picked in the latest
            sweep, the {data.counts.early_signals} early signals, the full registry and the watchlist.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="file" href="/funding/registry.csv">registry.csv</a>
          <span>Every call any sweep has reported, {data.counts.registry} so far, one line each: the date it was first
            seen, the funder, the programme, the deadline and the link. This is what decides what counts as new.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="file" href="/funding/watchlist.csv">watchlist.csv</a>
          <span>The {data.counts.watchlist} funders checked on every sweep: category, typical cycle, who may apply, and
            why each one is on the list.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Schedule</h2>
      <p>
        The sweep runs Monday and Friday at 02:51 New York time. The site picks up the brief at 13:37 UTC the same
        day, through <a href="https://github.com/aquastar/zhiqian-ai/blob/main/.github/workflows/funding-sync.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener">a
        scheduled job</a> whose parser is
        <a href="https://github.com/aquastar/zhiqian-ai/blob/main/scripts/build-funding.py" target="_blank" rel="noopener">in the repository</a>
        and fails the run rather than publish a personal field.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .container { max-width: min(95vw, 1600px); margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .doc { max-width: 820px; text-align: left; }
  .back { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: .8rem; }
  .back a { color: #475569; text-decoration: none; }
  .back a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .doc h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 8px; letter-spacing: -.02em; text-align: left; }
  .doc h2 { font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .1em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: #64748b; margin: 26px 0 8px; }
  .doc h3 { font-size: .95rem; margin: 0 0 3px; color: #0f172a; text-align: left; }
  .doc p, .doc li span { font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.65; color: #334155; text-align: left; }
  .lede { font-size: .95rem; }
  .lede b { white-space: nowrap; }
  .doc a { color: #1d4ed8; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(29,78,216,.3); }
  .doc a:hover { border-color: currentColor; }
  .layers { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .layers p { margin: 0; }
  .files { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .files li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 130px minmax(0,1fr); gap: 12px; align-items: baseline;
    padding: 10px 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.3); border-radius: 10px; background: #fff; }
  .doc a.file { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-weight: 700; font-size: .85rem;
    border-bottom: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .files li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
  }
</style>
